<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paraíba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paraíba is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> on the Atlantic coast, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-norte">Rio Grande do Norte</a> and Pernambuco, with its capital at João Pessoa. Founded as a Portuguese captaincy in 1585 to grow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, it was occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> between 1634 and 1654. It joined the Pernambucan revolt of 1817 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-equator">Confederation of the Equator</a> in 1824.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paraiba.jpg" alt="Paraíba" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SVG implementation by E2m · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_da_Para%C3%ADba.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
